        "procedure": "Primary route: Ce(NO3)3·6H2O (178 mg, 410 μmol) in methanol (3 mL) was added to (Et4N)(ccnm) (100 mg, 412 μmol) in methanol (2 mL). 1,10-Phenanthroline monohydrate (164 mg, 827 μmol) in methanol (2 mL) and NaHCO3 (34 mg, 404 μmol) in water (1 mL) were added, immediately forming a suspension. After 1 week, orange needle crystals were manually separated and washed with methanol (40 mg, 19%). Alternate route: Na2CO3 (22 mg, 208 μmol) in water (1 mL) was added to Ce(NO3)3·6H2O (89 mg, 206 μmol) in methanol (2 mL), giving a white precipitate; phen monohydrate (81 mg, 407 μmol) in methanol (2 mL) and (Et4N)(ccnm) (50 mg, 206 μmol) in methanol (1 mL) were added. After 1 month, orange crystals of 2Ce formed.",
